{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/626584-w20-changing-breeds-several-questions","id":626584,"title":"W20 - Changing breeds - Several questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-14T07:13:48-07:00","id":626584,"title":"W20 - Changing breeds - Several questions","content":"Hello everyone, i'm a long time OWoD player about to start his first game in the Werewolf subsetting (playng a Mokol\u00e8 to be exact).<br /> <br /> I have several questions that more experienced players / storytellers might be able to answer:<br /> <br /> <b>Manipulation penalty of the various forms:</b> When does it apply exactly? Is it &quot;always on&quot; or is included for iteraction with non-shapeshifter who are not accustomed to shifting? If that is the case, what about kinfolk? Intimidate rolls? If the penalty is expressed as -X (opposed to simply 0) does it means that a minimum of 1 applies? If not, can the attribute go in the negatives? Does having a 0 or negative Manipulation due to this penalty correspont to auto-failing all rolls based on it?<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance 0:</b> Following the above, i have a similar question for Appearance. This is particulary interesting since the &quot;Resplendant crest&quot; Archid characteristic gives +3 apperance in that form, wich is listed as having the attribute set at 0. Dos that mean that a Mokole with RC has Appearance 3 in Archid form, or does it mean he has a 0 or a (normal score +3) depending on the interlocutor?<br /> <br /> <b>Armor and unsoakable damage: </b>I assume that armor allows to soak normally unsoakable damage, when it makes sense (silver sword: yes, flamethrower: no). If this is the case, how is the &quot;Armored scales&quot; archid characteristic handled? What about the &quot;Armor of the Tortoise&quot; gift?<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts activation time: </b>When a gift states &quot;spends a turn in concentration&quot; (or another similar wording), is the character prevented to use rage to gain extra action for that turn?<br /> <br /> <b>Regaining rage:</b> It's just me or there is no listed way in W20 for Mokol\u00e8 (or other breeds apparently) to regain rage? Aren't they supposed to regain it when looking at the sun?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7294-docnessuno","user":"DocNessuno","date":". 08-14-2015, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7294-docnessuno","name":"DocNessuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:24:19-07:00","id":626613,"title":"","content":"Manipulation penalties explicitly do not count against Intimidation attempts you might make.<br /> <br /> The Resplendent Crest would give you Appearance 3; it's phrased the way it is because Feathers used to be on the list, and they gave you a flat Appearance of 3 in Archid.<br /> <br /> Armored Scales would probably be more likely to soak a flamethrower than silver and/or gold, especially seeing as how fire isn't unsoakable (and with Master of Fire, is almost ignorable), but it's up in the air. Armor of the Tortoise, however, certainly does this, as only Gifts that specifically mention silver work on it (and presumably gold for Mokole and Corax).<br /> <br /> Spending a turn in concentration would probably lead to being an exclusive action, but it ends up being the ST's decision. If the Gift required Gnosis, you definitely won't be able to do it unless you have Chaos Mechanics.<br /> <br /> The methods of regaining Rage were left out for most Fera. The Mokole Breedbook has a chart for it, but it's sort of confusing and doesn't apparently mention that you're supposed to take it as &quot;first time you see the sun in the day&quot;, which means that if you want to get into a fight, sleep until noon for the greatest Rage recovery (and also be in the tropics). The Makara and Zhong Lung regain all Rage every day upon waking for their season, but some lower amount by other seasons (never mentioned even in the breed book, but it might correspond roughly to the equivalent solar auspice per season, so it would be tremendous in summer and not so much in winter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:25:09-07:00","id":626907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/626584-w20-changing-breeds-several-questions?p=626613#post626613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manipulation penalties explicitly do not count against Intimidation attempts you might make.<br /> <br /> <br /> Armored Scales would probably be more likely to soak a flamethrower than silver and/or gold, especially seeing as how fire isn't unsoakable (and with Master of Fire, is almost ignorable), but it's up in the air. Armor of the Tortoise, however, certainly does this, as only Gifts that specifically mention silver work on it (and presumably gold for Mokole and Corax).<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so you can or cannot soak silver/gold with armor of tortoise? I didn't quite understand from the reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5268-tenrec","name":"Tenrec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:30:12-07:00","id":626975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenrec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/626584-w20-changing-breeds-several-questions?p=626907#post626907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, so you can or cannot soak silver/gold with armor of tortoise? I didn't quite understand from the reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Werewolf's soaking Gifts, unless it explicitly says otherwise, silver/gold/hongmu remains unsoakable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:02:34-07:00","id":627004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Manipulation penalty of the various forms:</b> When does it apply exactly? Is it &quot;always on&quot; or is included for iteraction with non-shapeshifter who are not accustomed to shifting? If that is the case, what about kinfolk? Intimidate rolls? If the penalty is expressed as -X (opposed to simply 0) does it means that a minimum of 1 applies? If not, can the attribute go in the negatives? Does having a 0 or negative Manipulation due to this penalty correspont to auto-failing all rolls based on it?<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance 0:</b> Following the above, i have a similar question for Appearance. This is particulary interesting since the &quot;Resplendant crest&quot; Archid characteristic gives +3 apperance in that form, wich is listed as having the attribute set at 0. Dos that mean that a Mokole with RC has Appearance 3 in Archid form, or does it mean he has a 0 or a (normal score +3) depending on the interlocutor? </div> </div> </div>I've usually found it best to ignore the social penalties. There are beings that care about your appearance (which means they usually run in fear anyway) and there are beings that don't care. In the latter case, I don't see why a Silver Fang Crinos can't be perceived as beautiful by other werewolves. As for Manipulation, the only explanation I've heard that makes sense is that it's harder to lie with body language, which is more emphasized in your beastly forms. If you buy into this, the Manipulation penalties should generally apply when you're somehow trying to project a particular image (which is always - that's one of the ways I differentiate Manipulation from Charisma).<br /> And then of course, there's the question whether the penalties should apply to Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T14:45:22-07:00","id":627988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocNessuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/626584-w20-changing-breeds-several-questions#post626584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, i'm a long time OWoD player about to start his first game in the Werewolf subsetting (playng a Mokol\u00e8 to be exact).<br /> <br /> I have several questions that more experienced players / storytellers might be able to answer:<br /> <br /> <b>Manipulation penalty of the various forms:</b> When does it apply exactly? Is it &quot;always on&quot; or is included for iteraction with non-shapeshifter who are not accustomed to shifting? If that is the case, what about kinfolk? Intimidate rolls? If the penalty is expressed as -X (opposed to simply 0) does it means that a minimum of 1 applies? If not, can the attribute go in the negatives? Does having a 0 or negative Manipulation due to this penalty correspont to auto-failing all rolls based on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Manipulation takes a hit for two reasons. One is physical - if your skull is suddenly radically different, with weird musculatue and vocal abilities, expressing yourself well is going to be a challenge. And then there's the mental side - the nonhuman forms are more &quot;instinctive,&quot; and express a great deal of their communication through body language. It's hard to not express yourself, or to control what you're expressing, and sometimes there's not even a desire to try.<br /> <br /> It applies across the board, except with Intimidation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Appearance 0:</b> Following the above, i have a similar question for Appearance. This is particulary interesting since the &quot;Resplendant crest&quot; Archid characteristic gives +3 apperance in that form, wich is listed as having the attribute set at 0. Dos that mean that a Mokole with RC has Appearance 3 in Archid form, or does it mean he has a 0 or a (normal score +3) depending on the interlocutor? </div> </div> </div>a changer retains their normal appearance score in the eyes of their own changing breed (and possibly others, though the Kitsune are the only ones hwere this is explicitly mentioned) A Mokole with the crest has Appearance 3 to outsiders, and Appearance +3 for Mokole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Armor and unsoakable damage: </b>I assume that armor allows to soak normally unsoakable damage, when it makes sense (silver sword: yes, flamethrower: no). If this is the case, how is the &quot;Armored scales&quot; archid characteristic handled? What about the &quot;Armor of the Tortoise&quot; gift? </div> </div> </div>As-written, no, becuase it is not explicitly &quot;armor&quot; it's just extra soak dice. Armor of the Tortice, on the other hand, was written explicitly as a form of armor in the breed book, and so I'd carry that over to modern iterations, unless stated otherwise<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Gifts activation time: </b>When a gift states &quot;spends a turn in concentration&quot; (or another similar wording), is the character prevented to use rage to gain extra action for that turn? </div> </div> </div>Yup, because actions (including those gained through Rage) take place <i>within</i> a turn. if you spend a whole turn doing something, that's what you spend it doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Regaining rage:</b> It's just me or there is no listed way in W20 for Mokol\u00e8 (or other breeds apparently) to regain rage? Aren't they supposed to regain it when looking at the sun? </div> </div> </div>it's covered in the Mokole breed book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}